11. MASTER DAG BRANCHING
============================================================

Some Master DAGs have conditional branching.

There are approximately:

- Maximum around 10 Master DAGs
- Around 300 child DAGs overall
- Only approximately 3-4 Master DAGs currently have complex branch
  decision logic

Manual maintenance is acceptable.

Example:

Oscar Master can have branches such as:

FIRST_DAY
SECOND_DAY
WEDNESDAY

The Master DAG has conditional logic.

The branch priority matters.

A representative logical priority is:

1. SECOND_DAY
2. WEDNESDAY
3. FIRST_DAY / DAILY

This means if conditions overlap, the actual Master DAG logic determines
which branch is selected.

Example:

If the 2nd day of the month happens to be Wednesday, the Master DAG should
select the appropriate higher-priority branch rather than executing the
same child multiple times.

