============================================================
16. EXAMPLE: MONTHLY DAG
============================================================

Suppose:

DAG:

job_A

Frequency:

Monthly

Schedule:

2nd day of every month


If today is:

1 September

Expected run:

2 September

The DAG should be considered a future expected job.

If today is:

2 September

and there is no execution:

NOT STARTED

If it starts:

IN PROGRESS

If it completes:

COMPLETED

If it fails:

FAILED

After the September cycle is successfully completed, the dashboard should
not continue to show it as NOT STARTED for the rest of September.

It should eventually be understood as:

WAITING FOR NEXT CYCLE

until the next expected execution cycle.

============================================================
17. EXAMPLE: WEEKLY DAG
============================================================

Suppose:

DAG:

job_B

Frequency:

Weekly

Schedule:

Every Wednesday

If today is Monday:

It is not expected to have run yet.

The dashboard should show the appropriate next expected date/cycle.

On Wednesday:

If no execution:
NOT STARTED

If running:
IN PROGRESS

If completed:
COMPLETED

If failed:
FAILED

After successful completion:

WAITING FOR NEXT CYCLE

until the next Wednesday cycle.

