31. DIRECTQUERY REQUIREMENT
============================================================

Power BI uses DirectQuery.

Therefore:

- Avoid unnecessary heavy transformations in Power BI.
- SQL/view performance matters.
- Avoid unnecessary joins or row multiplication.
- Avoid duplicate rows caused by branch mappings.
- Be careful because a child DAG can belong to multiple branches.

============================================================
32. DUPLICATION CHALLENGE
============================================================

One major technical/business challenge is:

A child DAG can exist under multiple branches.

Example:

oscar_cd_contributions_LRA

could have:

FIRST_DAY
WEDNESDAY
SECOND_DAY

in dag_branch_mapping_pbi.

The dashboard should not incorrectly show three independent expected
executions for the same child on a date when only one branch is actually
selected.

Branch priority and actual Master logic must be respected.

============================================================
33. PERIODIC EXPECTATION CHALLENGE
============================================================

The biggest business challenge is determining:

"Is this DAG expected to run now?"

A simple check such as:

frequency = MONTHLY

is not enough.

The system may need to know:

- Day of month
- Day of week
- Branch condition
- Branch priority
- Current month
- Current week
- Current cycle
- Whether the previous cycle completed
- Whether the next cycle has arrived
- Airflow next_run_time where available

============================================================
34. MASTER-TRIGGERED CHALLENGE
============================================================

For Master-triggered DAGs:

- Child DAG may have schedule = None.
- Airflow may not provide a meaningful next execution.
- The Master branch logic determines whether it is expected.
- Some child DAGs belong to multiple branches.
- Branch priority determines which branch is selected.
- The Master itself is not necessarily recorded in the execution audit.

Only a small number of Master DAGs have complex branching.

Manual metadata maintenance is acceptable.

